{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365915-wip-sorcerous-initiation-artifact-sorcerer-spirit-rings","id":1365915,"title":"[WiP] Sorcerous Initiation+Artifact: Sorcerer Spirit Rings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-06T19:07:05-08:00","id":1365915,"title":"[WiP] Sorcerous Initiation+Artifact: Sorcerer Spirit Rings","content":"Way back in the earliest days of 1Ed, in once o the first books,<i> the Book of Three Circles</i>, there were described Spirit Rings. If you don't remember, these were artifact jewelery that held the spirit of an ancient Sorcerer. Not really expanded upon then, I was thinking these would make an interesting possible Sorcerous Initiation in 3Ed rules. So, I finally got some work done on that aspect of it, and would like some feedback as I'm not sure how balanced this is. Please take a look and let me know what needs adjusted. And if you guys like this idea, I'll finish the fluff later<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerer Spirit Ring</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Shaping Rituals</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As long as the sorcerer is wearing the ring, he is always with the spirit within. And their Essences are linked. Thus, if the spirit is willing, he may assist when casting spells. Once per scene, the player may also roll the spirit\u2019s Intelligence to cast a spell along with the sorcerer's own dice. This effect applies to each roll of the casting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In life the spirit was once a knowledgeable sorcerer herself, and knew many spells. Using the link between them, the sorcerer wearing the ring can draw upon hat knowledge. Once per session, he may attempt to cast a spell he himself does not know but is known to the spirit. However, the cost in both sorcerous motes and willpower is doubled. Also, it is possible a failed casting may result in consequences similar to a botch. Note, the sorcerer may not attempt to cast spells from circles or sorcery he himself has not achieved as he would not be able to control such magics yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When wearing the ring, the sorcerer has his own will, but so does the spirit within. As such, he may draw upon the link between them to draw upon that power. Whenever the sorcerer ragains willpower if he gains more than he can have himself (puts him over his maximum temporary willpower), he can transfer the excess to the ring, up to the spirit\u2019s own limit. He may later use these points when casting spells. These points can only be used for spellcasting genrally, though it may be possible some rings could have special evocations that could also draw from this pool.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerous Mentor(4):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the spirit trapped inside the ring was once an expert in the arts of sorcery, and has knowledge of many spells, and about the world and times when he lived. As such, he can use the mental link with the ring\u2019s wearer to teach and aid the younger sorcerer. Taking this merit provides a free Lore specialty about the time period the spirit was familiar with. Also, when learning a new spell, one that the spirit himself knows, half the training time required.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">as an artifact , the ring will naturally have built in magics of its own. Often Occult, Lore, and casting aids, but not limited to these. Whatever they may be, they will reflect the personality of the spirit within as well as the wearer.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 02-07-2020, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T21:35:18-08:00","id":1365939,"title":"","content":"I feel like being able to cast a spell you don't know (even at a substantially increased cost) is a bit much for a shaping ritual -- a significant percentage of sorcery is cast when there's no time pressure anyway, after all. (The ability to do something similar is already a four-dot Merit in the Lunars book.)<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Mentor seems overpriced. I mean, for a four-dot Merit you could actually have the goremaul Asphodel, which I consider a lot better than a free Lore specialty and reduced training time (since it comes with a ghost who can teach the wielder all kinds of stuff about sorcery and the time in which he lived).<br /> <br /> I like the other bits, though. Speaking of Asphodel, these shaping rituals probably would work pretty well for someone who learned sorcery from Shou Ren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T23:53:51-08:00","id":1365953,"title":"","content":"ok, I was wondering if I overpowered that one. Got any ideas what I can replace it with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T23:59:13-08:00","id":1365955,"title":"","content":"Why does it cost less Merit dots to get a sorcerous mentor who is <i>not</i> a restless shade bound eternally to a piece of cold metal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T02:24:09-08:00","id":1365969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365915-wip-sorcerous-initiation-artifact-sorcerer-spirit-rings?p=1365955#post1365955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it cost less Merit dots to get a sorcerous mentor who is <i>not</i> a restless shade bound eternally to a piece of cold metal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because such a mentor has a life of their own, is not always with you, doesn't give a free Speciality...<br /> <br /> I'd replace being able to cast an unknown spell with having your Control Spell not count against the 1/scene limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-07-2020, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T02:57:49-08:00","id":1365976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365915-wip-sorcerous-initiation-artifact-sorcerer-spirit-rings?p=1365955#post1365955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it cost less Merit dots to get a sorcerous mentor who is <i>not</i> a restless shade bound eternally to a piece of cold metal?</div> </div> </div> </div>because I don't play much so don't have a good sense of game balance so mostly pull numbers out my ass and hope I did it right.<br /> <br /> I don't post often for a reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 02-07-2020, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T05:40:36-08:00","id":1365988,"title":"","content":"The first ritual looks fairly balanced to me. With intelligence 5, it's 2.5 motes/roll for a given spell, which probably averages 5-ish motes a scene, depending on how big the spell is. Sevenfold Art Invocation is 3-5 motes on a non-control spell 1/scene, plus 3-5 each time you cast a control spell. Terror-Relishing Art is (attribute)+(essence difference if positive) motes 1/scene, but only if you intimidate people.<br /> <br /> I think the second and third rituals might be better as merits - they give you more diverse capabilities, rather than give you sorcerous motes as most shaping rituals do.<br /> The second seems similar to Sage of Three Circles, but 1/session instead of 1/story, and doubling the cost. I'd say probably 4 or 5 dots as a merit.<br /> The third seems similar to a sphere of the revolutionary dog, but with a higher cap, only for sorcery, and not a hearthstone. Probably 3-4 dots as a merit.<br /> <br /> Ideas for alternative rituals<br /> The spirit has a Minor, Major and Defining intimacy. When you act according to them, you gain 1/2/3 sorcerous motes that last until you sleep. Casting a control spell in accordance with one of these intimacies adds 2 to this total. When you suffer for one of these intimacies enough to gain a willpower, increase the gain by (essence) [This is based on the derangement ritual from the scarred by nightmares initiation]<br /> You may bargain with the spirit, negotiating for an hour by rolling (charisma+presence) and gaining that many sorcerous motes. Offering some piece of occult knowledge the sorcerer didn't know before increases this by 1 mote, and offering a great occult secret increases it by 1. These last until you bargain again, or until the end of the story. This cannot be done more than once per day. [Based on the Heptagram and Wanansaan shaping rituals]<br /> Whenever you first reach some place, person or object of importance to the sorcerer's life, you gain 10 sorcerous motes, which last until the end of the story or this triggers again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T21:30:28-08:00","id":1369507,"title":"","content":"Hi, bringing this up again since I'm tinkering with this again (already changed the shaping rituals, will repost later), and an unsure which implementation is best for a new possible power. If I wanted to make it so the sorcerer gets the control spell benefits for the control spell the spirit once had, should that be a new Merit? Or an Evocation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}